+        """Demote warm blocks back to the free queue.
+
+        Always oldest-first (cold -> hot), in two phases:
+          Phase 1 -- evict blocks that have **exceeded** the current retention.
+          Phase 2 -- if still short, keep evicting from the head regardless of
+                     age, so the caller always gets its blocks.
+
+        Hot blocks are protected naturally: every hit moves them out of warm
+        via `touch()`, and the next release stamps them fresh at the back of the
+        queue, so they survive many eviction rounds while cold blocks age out
+        from the head.
+
+        Eviction clears the hash too (`_maybe_evict_cached_block`), after which
+        the block can no longer be hit by a prefix -- that is what "demote"
+        means here.
